// Plan stage R0k-b2 (form 4 with a capture; p03 of the design review of
// R0k, written so that the clause runs the value): the clause resumes,
// then runs `g`. `g` keeps `r`, a reference into `v`, a local of the
// handled body, which has ended at that time: W0301. The run in the clause
// gets a copy of the closure body; the copy reads `r` through the
// environment local of the region.
effect Run { fn run(g: fn()) }
fn main() {
    handle Run { fn run(g) { resume(())
        g() } } in {
        let v = Vec.new()
        v.push(1)
        let r = &v[0]
        run(|| print(r))
    }
}
